# Track H — AMD Metal 31001 wire (stage only, base 52f7298)

**Do not edit live** `amd_vega.py` / `amd_polaris.py` / `amd_legacy_gcn.py`.
MC applies after promoting `tahoe_iosurface_ca.py.stage-H`.

Verified against INTEGRATE `52f7298`: live `amd_vega.patches()` ends with
`**compositor_patches(...)` only — H wire is additive after that line.

## Import (once per file)

```python
from ...shared_patches.tahoe_iosurface_ca import iosurface_ca_patches
```

## Call sites (after compositor_patches)

```python
**compositor_patches(self._xnu_major, self._xnu_minor, self._constants.detected_os_version),
**iosurface_ca_patches(self._xnu_major, self._xnu_minor, self._constants.detected_os_version),
```

Targets: `amd_vega.py`, `amd_polaris.py` (both return paths that call compositor_patches),
`amd_legacy_gcn.py`.

## Parallel Track N

| Env | N Common IOSurface/QC | H surgical IOSurface/QC |
|-----|----------------------|-------------------------|
| unset | off | off |
| `X86_EXTREME=1` only | on (N filter) | off (needs CA latch) |
| `X86_EXTREME=1` + `X86_EXTREME_IOSURFACE_CA=1` | on | on (same payload IDs → idempotent) |
| `X86_TAHOE_NONMETAL=1` only | on | off |

### Conflict comment (N ioaccel vs H)
N IOAccelerator stage may set `IOSurface.kext=10.14.6` while H/Common use `10.15.7`.
MC: when H latch is active on Metal AMD, keep **10.15.7**; do not let ioaccel 10.14.6
win last-write if both patch sets apply.
